## ADR-0016: The true CI root cause — lock-dependent cache in setup-node — 2026-08-08
Context: all 18 workflow runs failed in 8-25s, including the first P0 scaffold,
which could not have failed on tests. Inspection showed setup-node's `cache: npm`
hashes for a lock file that has never existed, failing the run in setup before
any real step. ADR-0015's npm-install fix could not help because the cache step
runs *before* the npm step.
Decision: remove the cache entirely from setup-node in both workflows; install
with `npm install --no-audit --no-fund`; isolate Playwright e2e into its own job
so a browser/dev-server hiccup cannot block typecheck/build or Pages deploy.
Consequences: setup can no longer fail on the missing lock file; build/deploy
are independent of e2e stability. Supersedes ADR-0015.
